From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 08:04:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: samsung: Add the PLL_0817X and PLL_1018X types

Exynos9820 drives its shared PLLs with two IP revisions that the driver
does not name yet: PLL_0817X (fout_pll_shared0 and fout_pll_shared1) and
PLL_1018X (fout_pll_shared4).

Both belong to families the driver already handles. The vendor clock
abstraction layer puts them in the very same buckets as types that are
already supported: PLL_0817X shares its spec with PLL_0822X and
PLL_1017X, and PLL_1018X shares its spec with PLL_0818X
(cal-if/pll_spec.c:293-301 of
LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_exynos9820 at 7d08ec364a06). The two
specs describe the same register layout, an integer PLL with P in 1..63,
M in 64..1023, S in 0..6 and no K field (:158-177); they differ only in
the allowed input and VCO frequency ranges, which the clock driver does
not encode.

Since pll_0818x and pll_0822x already share samsung_pll0822x_clk_ops
with the same enable and lock bit offsets, add the two new names to that
same case list rather than duplicating the ops.

This is not a new idea: an out of tree Exynos9820 port carries the same
change, with the two names in the same ops group
(chiffathefox/exynos-9820-mainline-linux at 0aeca03f7acd,
drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.h and clk-pll.c). Landing it
upstream is what removes the need for a local "#define pll_0817x
pll_0818x" shim in every tree that wants to build an Exynos9820 clock
driver.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.c | 2 ++
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.h | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.c b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.c
index fdb84bcec91..61d90d53f0b 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.c
@@ -1649,6 +1649,7 @@ static void __init _samsung_clk_register_pll(struct samsung_clk_provider *ctx,
 	case pll_1418x:
 	case pll_1051x:
 	case pll_1052x:
+	case pll_0817x:
 	case pll_0818x:
 	case pll_0822x:
 	case pll_0516x:
@@ -1657,6 +1658,7 @@ static void __init _samsung_clk_register_pll(struct samsung_clk_provider *ctx,
 	case pll_0717x:
 	case pll_0718x:
 	case pll_0732x:
+	case pll_1018x:
 		pll->enable_offs = PLL0822X_ENABLE_SHIFT;
 		pll->lock_offs = PLL0822X_LOCK_STAT_SHIFT;
 		if (!pll->rate_table)
diff --git a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.h b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.h
index d6eb3246611..00bf34c0438 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.h
+++ b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.h
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@ enum samsung_pll_type {
 	pll_1451x,
 	pll_1452x,
 	pll_1460x,
+	pll_0817x,
 	pll_0818x,
 	pll_0822x,
 	pll_0831x,
@@ -50,6 +51,7 @@ enum samsung_pll_type {
 	pll_0732x,
 	pll_4311,
 	pll_1017x,
+	pll_1018x,
 	pll_1031x,
 	pll_a9fracm,
 	pll_a9fraco,
